{
  "analysis": "The ELF is 32-bit little-endian MIPS o32, entry 0x400110. The source shows framebuffer resolution 640x400, 32-bit RGBA. Strings reveal the binary expects to save frames to /tmp/frame.bmp and uses standard file operations. I need to find the DG_DrawFrame implementation, understand the exact syscall numbers/instructions used in the binary, and get the full program segment layout.",
  "plan": "Inspect the full doomgeneric.h, find DG_DrawFrame/DG_Init in the source, check the Makefile for build/platform details, and disassemble/search the binary for syscall instructions and imported symbols to determine which syscalls must be handled.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/doomgeneric.h\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -R \"DG_DrawFrame\\|DG_Init\\|DG_SetWindowTitle\\|frame.bmp\\|void DG\" -n /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric | head -60\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/Makefile\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "readelf -l /app/doomgeneric_mips\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "objdump -d /app/doomgeneric_mips | grep -E \"syscall|break|lwc0|swc0\" | head -50\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "readelf -s /app/doomgeneric_mips | grep -Ei \"open|read|write|close|exit|brk|mmap|lseek|fstat|stat|DG_|main|_start\" | head -80\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
